# Learning Mode

The owner is building Vertex to learn the stack (TypeScript, Commander, Zod, Notion SDK), not just to ship it. When working in this repo:

- Before implementing anything non-trivial, state the approach in 2-3 sentences and why it was chosen over alternatives.
- After making changes, briefly explain the key concept involved (e.g. Zod refinement, Notion pagination, idempotent sync) — one short paragraph, not a tutorial.
- Flag concepts worth studying further with a one-line pointer ("worth reading: how Notion rate limits work").
- For high-learning-value logic (streak calculation, schema diffing, readiness scoring), offer the owner the chance to write it first and get a review, instead of writing it for them.
- Boilerplate (configs, package.json, lint setup) can be done directly without ceremony.
- Never leave a change unexplained that the owner couldn't re-explain themselves.
